          "id": "chatgpt_plan.background_use",
          "required": true,
          "text": "gobble signs in to your ChatGPT plan under its own name, \"gobble\".\nIt stores the access, refresh and ID tokens, your account id and this host's id, in auth.json in gobble's config directory on this machine, readable by you alone, and sends them only to OpenAI.\nThis machine must be one only you control, never a shared or managed one. Do not copy auth.json to another machine.\nTo remove the sign-in, run gobble auth logout openai, which also revokes it at OpenAI.\nBackground requests, a session's title and automatic compaction, run under your plan only if you allow them; gobble auth consent openai background deny withdraws that at any time.\nOn another device, open the address shown, sign in there, then paste here the address the browser lands on.\n\nAllow gobble to make background requests under your ChatGPT plan: naming sessions and compacting them on its own?",
          "links": [
            {
              "rel": "usage",
              "url": "https://chatgpt.com/settings/usage"
